:{"animal":1},"evidence_level":"animal","eco":{"id":"ECO:0007120","label":"animal model system study evidence"},"oxford":{"level":"5","label":"bench or animal research"},"evidence_lines":[{"design":"animal","eco":{"id":"ECO:0007120","label":"animal model system study evidence"},"mesh_publication_types":[],"papers":1,"pmids":["39150493"]}],"pmids":["39150493"]}],"years":{"from":1981,"to":2026},"basis":"MeSH indexing and publication types of the most relevant PubMed records; counts are of papers in the sample, not findings.","vocabulary":{"evidence_type":"ECO (Evidence & Conclusion Ontology)","study_design":"MeSH Publication Types","strength":"Oxford CEBM 2009 levels","structure":"SEPIO assertion / evidence line / evidence item"},"search_url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/?term=Germacrene%20B%5BAll%20Fields%5D"},"trials":{"total":0,"matched_loosely":0,"studies":[],"source":"ClinicalTrials.gov","search_url":"https://clinicaltrials.gov/search?intr=Germacrene%20B"},"is_terpenoid":false,"consumer_summary":{"model":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","generated":"2026-09-11","what_it_is":"Germacrene B is a volatile sesquiterpene, a type of aromatic molecule that plants use to communicate and defend themselves. It acts as a crucial building block in nature, serving as a central intermediate that plants use to synthesize a wide variety of other complex terpenes. You might encounter its earthy, woody scent in the essential oils of various medicinal herbs and flowers.","found_in":"It is naturally produced by a wide array of plants, including the chaste tree (Vitex agnus-castus), Surinam cherry (Eugenia uniflora), and the common daisy (Bellis perennis). It has also been identified in the complex terpene profiles of Cannabis sativa.","why_researchers_care":"Researchers are fascinated by Germacrene B because of its foundational role in plant chemistry and its potential biological activity in humans. Much of the current interest centers on its ability to fight off microbes and oxidative stress, as well as its intriguing function as an insect pheromone. The strongest evidence so far comes from human observational studies (Oxford level 2b), which are guiding scientists toward understanding how this versatile molecule might be harnessed for health and pest control.","structure_function":[{"claim_id":"antimicrobial","statement":"Early observational work points toward Germacrene B having properties that may support the body's defense against bacterial and fungal threats.","evidence_level":"human_observational","basis":"This rests on 26 papers, including human observational and in vitro studies.","eco":{"id":"ECO:0000180","label":"clinical study evidence"},"oxford":{"level":"2b","label":"individual cohort or observational study"},"evidence_lines":[{"design":"human_observational","eco":"ECO:0000180","papers":7},{"design":"animal","eco":"ECO:0007120","papers":1},{"design":"in_vitro","eco":"ECO:0000181","papers":12}],"paper_count":26},{"claim_id":"antioxidant","statement":"Observational research suggests it may support cellular health by acting as an antioxidant to neutralize free radicals.","evidence_level":"human_observational","basis":"This is based on 18 papers across observational, animal, and lab designs.","eco":{"id":"ECO:0000180","label":"clinical study evidence"},"oxford":{"level":"2b","label":"individual cohort or observational study"},"evidence_lines":[{"design":"human_observational","eco":"ECO:0000180","papers":6},{"design":"animal","eco":"ECO:0007120","papers":2},{"design":"in_vitro","eco":"ECO:0000181","papers":3}],"paper_count":18},{"claim_id":"anti-inflammatory","statement":"The molecule is being studied for its potential to support healthy inflammatory responses.","evidence_level":"human_observational","basis":"This is supported by 6 papers, including human observational and animal research.","eco":{"id":"ECO:0000180","label":"clinical study evidence"},"oxford":{"level":"2b","label":"individual cohort or observational study"},"evidence_lines":[{"design":"human_observational","eco":"ECO:0000180","papers":1},{"design":"animal","eco":"ECO:0007120","papers":2},{"design":"in_vitro","eco":"ECO:0000181","papers":1}],"paper_count":6},{"claim_id":"insect","statement":"Early work points toward its utility in pest management, specifically as an insect repellent or pheromone disruptor.","evidence_level":"human_observational","basis":"This rests on 3 papers, including observational and animal studies.","eco":{"id":"ECO:0000180","label":"clinical study evidence"},"oxford":{"level":"2b","label":"individual cohort or observational study"},"evidence_lines":[{"design":"human_observational","eco":"ECO:0000180","papers":1},{"design":"animal","eco":"ECO:0007120","papers":2}],"paper_count":3},{"claim_id":"digestive","statement":"Animal research indicates it may support healthy digestive function.","evidence_level":"animal","basis":"This is based on 2 animal studies.","eco":{"id":"ECO:0007120","label":"animal model system study evidence"},"oxford":{"level":"5","label":"bench or animal research"},"evidence_lines":[{"design":"animal","eco":"ECO:0007120","papers":2}],"paper_count":2}],"hypothesized_benefits":[{"claim_id":"antimicrobial","area":"Antimicrobial action","hypothesis":"Researchers are exploring whether Germacrene B can effectively inhibit the growth of resistant bacteria and fungi in human infections.","evidence_level":"human_observational","paper_count":26,"study_to_test_it":"A randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled human clinical trial applying a topical Germacrene B formulation to superficial bacterial skin infections, measuring bacterial load and healing time over 14 days.","eco":{"id":"ECO:0000180","label":"clinical study evidence"},"oxford":{"level":"2b","label":"individual cohort or observational study"},"evidence_lines":[{"design":"human_observational","eco":"ECO:0000180","papers":7},{"design":"animal","eco":"ECO:0007120","papers":1},{"design":"in_vitro","eco":"ECO:0000181","papers":12}]},{"claim_id":"cancer","area":"Cellular health","hypothesis":"Observational data has led researchers to investigate whether this terpene might influence cellular proliferation and survival.","evidence_level":"human_observational","paper_count":9,"study_to_test_it":"A randomized controlled trial in high-risk human cohorts evaluating the effect of a standardized Germacrene B supplement on specific blood biomarkers of cellular proliferation over six months.","eco":{"id":"ECO:0000180","label":"clinical study evidence"},"oxford":{"level":"2b","label":"individual cohort or observational study"},"evidence_lines":[{"design":"human_observational","eco":"ECO:0000180","papers":9}]},{"claim_id":"anti-inflammatory","area":"Inflammation","hypothesis":"Early animal and observational work points toward a potential role in modulating inflammatory pathways, which could be valuable for managing chronic inflammatory states.","evidence_level":"human_observational","paper_count":6,"study_to_test_it":"A randomized, placebo-controlled human trial administering oral Germacrene B to healthy adults with elevated baseline C-reactive protein (CRP), measuring systemic inflammatory markers over 8 weeks.","eco":{"id":"ECO:0000180","label":"clinical study evidence"},"oxford":{"level":"2b","label":"individual cohort or observational study"},"evidence_lines":[{"design":"human_observational","eco":"ECO:0000180","papers":1},{"design":"animal","eco":"ECO:0007120","papers":2},{"design":"in_vitro","eco":"ECO:0000181","papers":1}]},{"claim_id":"pain","area":"Pain management","hypothesis":"If early animal findings bear out, Germacrene B might offer a novel natural pathway for soothing pain and discomfort.","evidence_level":"animal","paper_count":1,"study_to_test_it":"A first-in-human, double-blind, crossover study evaluating acute pain thresholds using a cold-pressor test after a single oral dose of Germacrene B compared to placebo.","eco":{"id":"ECO:0007120","label":"animal model system study evidence"},"oxford":{"level":"5","label":"bench or animal research"},"evidence_lines":[{"design":"animal","eco":"ECO:0007120","papers":1}]}],"associated_conditions":[],"cautions":null,"evidence_at_a_glance":"Best evidence so far is human observational work (Oxford 2b); most of the rest is animal and lab research exploring its foundational chemical properties."}}
